No `model.py` training changes are needed. FP16 forward and FP32/BF16 training paths remain as they were. Public `inference_window_block_cached` is the packed-weight FP8 API; its input storage may still be Half. `prepare_window_cached_weight` leaves Half weights unchanged. Preparation returns an ordinary contiguous tensor when the compiled policy has no cache route for the current SM.

## Snapshot bookkeeping

Prepared blocks register the full cache and keep each existing canonical weight name as cache[0]. This avoids a third physical copy and preserves generic operator paths. The `InferenceBlock._apply` hook restores canonical aliases after whole-model or direct-block moves. Actual allocated packed-weight bytes count distinct storage allocations rather than counting aliases twice. Prepared snapshots should be recreated after source-model updates.

## Continuous tuning

`run_tuning.py window-cached-range --manifest-only` enumerates every integer input size from1280×720 through3840×2160. The CPU scan found3,690,401 inputs,931 padded geometries,7,212 exact dispatch keys and67,032 physical cases including both timing orders. Actual block/shape memberships are retained; no cross-product of unrelated block and shape lists is constructed.

The draft runner reuses the resident all-peer benchmark harnesses, excludes cache preparation from timing, journals every completed physical case in SQLite and preserves failures. Resume identity pins GPU/binary, checkpoint, harness/source hashes, timing settings, complete requested membership, driver/Torch/CUDA versions and compiled policy versions. Volatile timestamps and free-memory fields are excluded. A complete sweep can be promoted explicitly with `window-cached-generate`; incomplete graph membership fails promotion. No continuous GPU sweep was run for this draft.

## Same-binary network benchmark

`tests/benchmark_window_cached_model.py.draft` captures two complete-model graphs using one prepared model and the same cache weights. During baseline capture only, a try/finally context redirects the public cached-window API to its canonical fallback. The public API is restored before candidate capture. Both graphs are captured before either is timed; normal and reversed timing rounds retain the same outputs and call counts.

The head is FP32 with four channels. Output budget is per graph, with combined retained bytes reported explicitly; captured shape, dtype and byte count are asserted. Every retained head is checked against the baseline, poisoned before three replays, and compared again after timing. Inputs and weights are also checked for mutation. This is a network-only resident comparison, not a renderer or native-DLL performance result.

## CPU validation and remaining execution gates

Forty CPU tests passed, including policy rejection/ranking/clamps, all-model and direct-block alias restoration, exact graph membership, resume rejection after runtime changes, benchmark substitution restoration and compiled-policy metadata collection. The full continuous geometry scan completed on CPU.

The public C++ files have not been built or executed by this subagent. Root must still run the public/graph tests, sanitizers, same-binary full-network benchmark and fresh native comparisons after activation. Existing v27 component evidence does not establish new public-route or full-model performance by itself. No85% hardware roofline or DLL speed claim is made here.
